      "text": "The distance between two points $(x_1, y_1)$ and $(x_2, y_2)$ in a Cartesian plane can be calculated using the distance formula:\n\\begin{align*}\nd &= \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}.\n\\end{align*}\nPlugging in the coordinates of the given points, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\nd &= \\sqrt{(4 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - (-4))^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(7)^2 + (-1)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{49 + 1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{50} \\\\\n&= \\boxed{5\\sqrt{2}}.\n\\end{align*}\nThe answer is: 5\\sqrt{2}",
